{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794752347,"nonce":"fe07DTKX5Ff4iPo6JxONtTrGMTQ=","title":"Web: Haxe programs in a browser, with each Rust library compiled to wasm","message":"A library stays the Rust crate it is on every other runtime; in a browser it is a wasm build, and the Haxe program is its frontend. Three program forms, each reaching the browser's APIs (WebGPU, the canvas, audio) its own way:\n\n| Program | Library build | Browser APIs from Rust | State |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| hxcpp through Emscripten | wasm32-unknown-emscripten, linked in | Emscripten's bindings; for WebGPU the emdawnwebgpu port's webgpu.h | builds and runs under node and, with `--browser`, in headless Chrome |\n| Ash wasm | dylink.0 side module | an `ash_host_agent` mailbox to a JS shim | runs under `ash run`; Ash's browser host untried (9ee1bd4) |\n| Haxe's JS target | wasm32-unknown-unknown through wasm-bindgen | web-sys | no adapter yet |\n\nOrder: hxcpp through Emscripten first (hxn-gpu-webgpu over webgpu.h, 5b1345d), then Ash's browser host, then the JS adapter.\n\nDone for Emscripten:\n- The inbox's turns under Emscripten run from the host's event loop (`emscripten_async_call`), so a future settled by a JavaScript callback after `main` returns is delivered. Before, the turns were re-queued on the Haxe event loop, which spun and kept the page's and Node's callbacks from running: the timer test hung under node.\n- `hxn run|check cpp --wasm --browser` writes the page (hxcpp's HXCPP_LINK_EMSCRIPTEN_EXT=.html and HXCPP_LINK_EMRUN) and serves it with emrun to headless Chrome; HXN_BROWSER and HXN_BROWSER_ARGS choose the browser and its flags. emrun prints its own lines on stdout, so the page's output goes through --log-stdout and --log-stderr files that hxn prints afterwards.\n- tests/web: a library whose future a JavaScript timer settles (emscripten_async_call), checked under node and in Chrome; CI runs both in the emscripten job.\n\nStill open for Emscripten:\n- `await` on a pending future blocks the page; only `then` delivers there.\n- Haxe's own event loop still sleeps on the main thread for timers (haxe.Timer.delay), which blocks a page the same way.\n- hxcpp's collector does not return from `Gc.run(true)` under Emscripten (9ee1bd4).","files":null}]}